.TH DTC_BINARY_FILE_COMPARE 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
DTC_binary_file_compare \- compare two DTC binary files event by event
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B DTC_binary_file_compare
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.I file1 file2
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads both files, matches data blocks by event-window tag, subsystem, DTC and
ROC, and logs every disagreement
.RB ( "Disagreement found! TS ..." )
and the counts of unmatched events at warning/info level through TLOG.
Does not open any device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Usage, exit 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Comparison completed (differences do not change the status); also when fewer
than two files are given (the usage routine exits 0 before the intended
.BR exit(1) ).
.TP
.B 2
A file cannot be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
DTC_binary_file_compare a.bin b.bin 2>&1 | grep Disagreement
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR data_file_verifier (1),
.BR binary_dump_to_DTC_file (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e TDAQ group (Eric Flumerfelt, Ryan Rivera, Ron Rechenmacher and others).
